Corrected Training Plan (Aligned to THIS Dataset)
1. Data Loading & Basic Temporal Validation
•	Load Walmart weekly sales dataset 
•	Inspect schema and datatypes 
•	Parse Date 
•	Sort by Store and Date 
•	Validate weekly temporal ordering 
•	Detect duplicate (Store, Date) records 
•	Verify weekly frequency consistency 
•	Check missing weeks per store 
________________________________________
2. Dataset Understanding
•	Define target: Weekly_Sales 
•	Identify exogenous variables: 
o	Temperature 
o	Fuel_Price 
o	CPI 
o	Unemployment 
o	Holiday_Flag 
•	Define forecasting horizon: 
o	1-week ahead forecasting 
•	Identify causal vs non-causal features 
________________________________________
3. Data Quality Checks
•	Missing value analysis 
•	Negative sales detection 
•	Outlier sales spikes 
•	Holiday consistency checks 
•	Sudden regime shift detection 
•	Store-level distribution consistency 
________________________________________
4. Exploratory Time-Series Analysis
•	Store-wise sales visualization 
•	Trend analysis 
•	Seasonality analysis 
•	Rolling averages 
•	Rolling variance 
•	STL decomposition 
•	ACF/PACF analysis 
Useful formulas:
yt=Tt+St+Rty_t = T_t + S_t + R_tyt=Tt+St+Rt
________________________________________
5. Temporal Feature Engineering
Core features:
Lag Features
•	Sales lag 1 
•	Sales lag 4 
•	Sales lag 12 
•	Sales lag 52 
Example:
Lagk=yt−kLag_k = y_{t-k}Lagk=yt−k
Rolling Features
•	Rolling mean 
•	Rolling std 
•	Rolling min/max 
Example:
RollingMeank=1k∑i=1kyt−iRollingMean_k = \frac{1}{k}\sum_{i=1}^{k} y_{t-i}RollingMeank=k1∑i=1kyt−i
Calendar Features
•	Month 
•	Quarter 
•	Week-of-year 
•	Holiday flag 
Trend Features
•	Expanding mean 
•	Time index 
________________________________________
6. Missing Data Handling
•	Forward fill exogenous variables if needed 
•	Interpolation for macroeconomic indicators 
•	Missingness indicators 
•	Leakage-safe imputation 
________________________________________
7. Outlier Handling
•	Store-wise anomaly detection 
•	Seasonal-aware outlier detection 
•	Winsorization experiments 
•	Robust scaling comparison 
________________________________________
8. Feature Selection
•	Correlation analysis 
•	Lag importance analysis 
•	Permutation importance 
•	Multicollinearity checks 
________________________________________
9. Dataset Splitting (CRITICAL)
DO NOT use random split.
Use:
•	Time-based train/validation/test split 
•	Expanding-window validation 
•	Rolling-window validation 
Correct temporal split:
Train<Validation<TestTrain < Validation < TestTrain<Validation<Test
________________________________________
10. Baseline Forecasting Models
•	Last-value baseline 
•	Seasonal naive baseline 
•	Moving average baseline 
Example:
y^t+1=yt\hat{y}_{t+1}=y_ty^t+1=yt
________________________________________
11. Machine Learning Models
Recommended:
•	Linear Regression 
•	Ridge/Lasso 
•	Random Forest 
•	XGBoost/LightGBM 
•	CatBoost 
•	Gradient Boosting 
Optional:
•	ARIMA/SARIMA 
•	Prophet 
Not recommended initially:
•	Transformers 
•	Complex deep learning models 
Dataset is too small for heavy neural architectures.
________________________________________
12. Evaluation
Use:
•	RMSE 
•	MAE 
•	MAPE 
•	WMAPE 
Example:
RMSE=1n∑i=1n(yi−y^i)2RMSE = \sqrt{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(y_i-\hat{y}_i)^2}RMSE=n1∑i=1n(yi−y^i)2
Also evaluate:
•	Per-store performance 
•	Holiday-period performance 
•	Residual autocorrelation 
•	Stability across time